        "original_id": "b76183b2-55bd-5963-939c-680b3dd427b2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Terry Kilgore\n- Places: Cumberland Gap\n- Roles: Virginia House of Delegates, Commerce and Labor committee\n- Topics: Republican Party, Appalachian Mountains, Cumberland Mountains\n\nFacts:\n- Terry Kilgore is a Republican.\n- Terry Kilgore was elected to the Virginia House of Delegates in 1993.\n- Terry Kilgore became chair of the Commerce and Labor committee in 2008.\n- The Cumberland Gap is a narrow pass through the long ridge of the Cumberland Mountains.\n- The Cumberland Gap is within the Appalachian Mountains.\n- The Cumberland Gap is near the junction of Kentucky, Virginia, and Tennessee.",
